{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/513771-considering-promethean-for-a-chat-rpg-game","id":513771,"title":"Considering Promethean for a chat rpg game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-13T21:36:32-07:00","id":513771,"title":"Considering Promethean for a chat rpg game.","content":"Hey all, I've been mulling over which 2e game to do for a while come september when we reset the chat i ST/Admin. And I've never played Promethean, but i started to really get into what I was reading about it. I purchased the Anthology and i've almost finished reading that to get me in the mindset. Part of me believes it would be a difficult game to run in a chat setting, but the other part sees their determination to understand humanity as a reason it could work too. That said, I don't even know if Promethean will be released by September, so I might be getting excited for no reason. <br /> <br /> I wanted to ask some of you who know the game better a few questions. Is it worth purchasing the old book? Will they be similar enough that I wouldn't get bad ideas about what to expect in my head? I have found the other 2e books somewhat similar in content. Could wasteland and disquiet work in a smaller scale if you wanted it to, such as in a huge city moving place to place within it? Is there a half splat like many of the other games? Do they allow you to play creators and their alchemies, because i think that would be cool.<br /> <br /> thanks for the listen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4024-storysanctum","name":"storysanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T05:16:37-07:00","id":514044,"title":"","content":"I think you'd better wait for a second edition. Don't get me wrong, I have all the Promethean material here at home on my shelf and it's the only game line for which I hunted down the screen and the character pads. The real problem with first edition was its mechanics. Let's just say they were not quite on par with other game lines and that a few errors went past editing.<br /> <br /> As far as wasteland and Disquiet goes, Mortal Remains had a quick reforge of these systems and I thought it worked well. The other option for you and your players is to use these things as dramatic effects rather than passive mechanics.<br /> <br /> So, why should you buy the first ed books?<br /> -Because they are filled with ideas about what it means to be a non-living-nor-dead proto-person<br /> -Because they explore the world of darkness with a hopeful eye<br /> -Because they are good readings<br /> -Because there are adventures at the end of them which combine to form a chronicle (the adventure's good and fitting for the 2nd edition, in my opinion)<br /> <br /> Why shouldn't you buy the books?<br /> -Because they are mechanically weird at a few points<br /> -Because when 2nd edition will come around you'll skip a few chapters thinking you've already read those in 1st","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T13:37:59-07:00","id":514436,"title":"","content":"1e will do you fine, though obviously it's not up to GMC standards, and there's no guarantee it'll be available in the timeframe you're working. It's still a frustrating book, and a lot of folks don't see it as playable in its current state, or even like half of what's in it. I haven't read the anthology, so I'm a bit clueless to how the new material confuses the old, so, grain of salt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T22:20:00-07:00","id":517651,"title":"","content":"Thanks, all of this has been helpful. I've had the Mortal Remains book to get a teaser of them, I went and got the 1e book and I've also started to consider a back up. I really enjoy the themes of Promethean, as we're combining two splats in a cross-supernatural chat game. Vampire being the other. I feel like Vampires and Prometheans share an estranged need or...desire for humanity. And that their themes have some religious resemblance as well as thematic. Both sharing rebirth, though Prometheans are no longer dead. But I also like their differences. How one is a struggle to feel and relate. One is trying not to tarnish or lose their ability to feel and relate. Anyways. I'll keep digging too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4024-storysanctum","name":"storysanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}